I replaced the null-check branch with a conditional pointer to a static zero, eliminating the unpredictable null branch while preserving the bounds check. This reduces branch mispredictions when decoding fields that lack a profile.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    static const decltype(profile->numFields) zero = 0;
    const auto *numFields = profile ? &profile->numFields : &zero;
    if (profileIndex >= *numFields)
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return profile->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```